vultr:index/kubernetes:Kubernetes.description:
Get information about a Vultr Kubernetes Engine (VKE) Cluster.

> The node pool deployed with this resource adds its own <span pulumi-lang-nodejs="`tag`" pulumi-lang-dotnet="`Tag`" pulumi-lang-go="`tag`" pulumi-lang-python="`tag`" pulumi-lang-yaml="`tag`" pulumi-lang-java="`tag`" pulumi-lang-hcl="`tag`">`tag`</span> which is then used as an identifier for Terraform to see which node pool is part of this resource. This resource only supports a single node pool. To deploy additional worker nodes you must use <span pulumi-lang-nodejs="`vultr.KubernetesNodePools`" pulumi-lang-dotnet="`vultr.KubernetesNodePools`" pulumi-lang-go="`KubernetesNodePools`" pulumi-lang-python="`KubernetesNodePools`" pulumi-lang-yaml="`vultr.KubernetesNodePools`" pulumi-lang-java="`vultr.KubernetesNodePools`" pulumi-lang-hcl="`vultr_kubernetes_node_pools`">`vultr.KubernetesNodePools`</span>.

